WHAT THIS COVERS
================

The datasets built for this project, and the experiment logs in ../results/:

  - ojsm-synthetic/            Frankenstein, Stolen DOI, Plausible and
                               Nonsense fabrication sets, constructed here
  - the real-citation sets     arXiv CS (2024), the CrossRef random sample,
                               and the Nature article references, collected
                               here
  - manifest.json
  - ../results/                every experiment log and re-check produced by
                               this project

You may copy, redistribute, adapt and build on this material for any purpose,
including commercially, provided you give appropriate credit. Cite the
repository (see ../CITATION.cff) and, where a figure or number is involved,
the run directory under ../results/ that produced it.

The code in this repository is licensed separately and more restrictively —
AGPL-3.0 with the Commons Clause. See ../LICENSE. The distinction is
deliberate: the tool carries a no-sale condition so that verification
infrastructure for the scholarly record stays free to use, while the evidence
behind the published claims carries none, because a reader who cannot freely
re-analyse the data cannot check the argument.


WHAT THIS DOES NOT COVER
========================

Three datasets are other researchers' work. They are NOT redistributed here
and are NOT licensed by this file. Each is fetched from its source on demand;
see README.md.

  - citeaudit-benchmark/, citeaudit-realworld/, citeaudit-realworld-subset/
      Shi, Sun, Zhang, Sun, Chawla & Ye (2026), arXiv:2602.23452
      https://github.com/shiiiikw/CiteAudit
      That repository carries no licence, so all rights are reserved to its
      authors. A licence request was sent 2026-08-04; this file will be
      updated if terms are granted.

  - compound-deception-ansari/
      Derived from the public GPTZero NeurIPS 2025 hallucination table
      referenced by Ansari (2026). Terms of reuse unstated.

The README.md files inside those directories record provenance only. Anything
this project derived from them — parsed BibTeX, our own labels, our own
results — is rebuilt locally by the importers in ../scripts/ and is not
distributed.
